extraction_notes: "WB20 Canada printed 86-88 (cache p087-p089, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer; printed 87 is a full-page illustration and printed 86 and 88 were rendered and read beside the text. Heading Tundra Ranger Cavalry O.C.C. on printed 86, stat block headed Tundra Ranger Cavalry O.C.C. (also known as the Tundra Riders and Mounties); it resumes at Psionics on printed 88. || GROUP: the book has no Men at Arms heading; the chapter is The Tundra Rangers (printed 78-90) and the entry is the Mounted Division of a para-military force, so occ_group is men-of-arms and men_of_arms is true. The entry prints no S.D.C. base; +3D6+6 S.D.C. is listed under O.C.C. bonuses and is stored as a pool bonus. || XP: the Anti-Robot Headhunter, Tundra Ranger Cavalry and Ixion Cyber-Horsemen ladder on printed 192, as supplied from a render. || BONUSES: +2 P.P., +2 initiative, +2 roll, +1 pull punch stored; +1 vs cold is stored as saves.other. The text layer prints the Horror Factor levels as 2,4,1, 10 and 13; the render of printed 88 reads 2, 4, 7, 10 and 13, stored as five at_level entries. || RACE-CONDITIONAL, not stored as numbers: American/English is -18% for Simvan, and Simvan, Psi-Stalkers and other D-Bees read at 60% +1% per level instead of 84%; both are in the skill notes. The Racial Restrictions note that Simvan and Psi-Stalker Cavalry Rangers use these skills in place of their R.C.C. skills is a restrictions line and is not enforced. || SKILL READINGS: Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic; Speaks American/English at 98% is Language: Native Tongue; Literate in American at 84% +1% per level is Literacy: Native Language at 84 with per_level 1; Herd Cattle is Herding Cattle; Lore: Cattle/Animals is Lore: Cattle & Animals; Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals; Tracking (humanoids) is Tracking (people); Swim and Climb are Swimming and Climbing. Horsemanship: Cowboy, Horsemanship: Exotic Animals and Trick Riding carry no printed bonus and are stored at the catalog figures. Hand to Hand: Expert, Martial Arts or Assassin (if Anarchist or evil) for two related skills. || RELATED: Electrical Basic only is Basic Electronics; Mechanical is Basic Mechanics only; Science is Astronomy and Mathematics: Advanced; Pilot except robots, ships and aircraft excludes the robot and power armor rows, Boat: Ships, the submersible and warship rows, and every aircraft and spacecraft row; Jet Packs, hovercycles and Military: Tanks & APCs stay available (a reading). This book files riding under Pilot, so the catalog Horsemanship category is offered as General and Exotic Animals only. || EQUIPMENT: Standard Equipment, Vehicle and Money all say Standard and point at Notes on the Tundra Rangers, printed 82-83, so that list is stored: Legion Tundra armor and the thermal-armor suit (catalog rows from this book), six E-Clips, a Vibro-Blade as a pick of three since the book names no kind, two field uniforms, a dress uniform, cleated insulated combat boots, casual and dress clothing, thermal gloves on the plain gloves row, the high-impact helmet with built-in communicator on the communications-helmet row, tinted goggles, the 100 feet of nylon cord on the cord row, utility belt, scarf, air filter, backpack, bedroll, duffle bag or saddlebag as a pick, flashlight, distancing binoculars, language translator, note pad, 1D4 markers, 1D4 signal flares, two canteens, 6 weeks of rations as six of the week-sized food-rations row, first aid kit, and a horse or hovercycle as a pick (printed 83: a horse or hovercycle are pretty standard). NOT stored, no catalog row: the energy rifle itself and one weapon with two E-Clips for each W.P. (the book names no models; printed 187 points at the core book early Coalition weapons), dress boots, pick-hatchet, tundra survival kit, 20 climbing anchors, small M.D.C. ceramic mallet, web vest, winter cap. The multi-optics goggle is a special request, not issue, and is left out. || MONEY: Standard is a salary of 1500 credits per month plus room, board and gear (printed 83); the book prints no starting savings, so one month of salary is stored as starting_money, a reading. The Cavalry mount is the same pick; 57% ride an exotic animal and 20% a bionic or robot horse (Rifts New West), which the book does not issue as starting kit. || The Code of the Tundra Rangers (printed 81) is paraphrased in the body. The list Other Common O.C.C.s available to Tundra Rangers on printed 88 is a pointer list, not part of this class."
