## Lore

The Mounted Division is the least human part of the Tundra Rangers. Simvan
Monster Riders, Psi-Stalkers, Ixion and ordinary Centaurs and a good many
Native American horsemen fill its ranks, drawn together by a love of riding
and a way with animals. Every member has the same basic training as any
other Ranger; the specialty is the saddle.

All of them are expert on horseback, but more than half ride something
stranger, such as a Rhino-Buffalo, a bison or a dinosaur, and a fifth ride
bionic or robot horses. That makes the Cavalry the wildest looking and most
alarming division the Rangers field. The Simvan are excused the standard
uniform and armor, which they find confining; nearly everyone else wears the
white armor with pride.

Old hatreds, Simvan against Psi-Stalker and Simvan against human, are set
aside for the cause. The Simvan stay short on patience and the Psi-Stalkers
tease everyone, but in a fight they stand together and risk their lives for
each other. Wilderness folk call the Cavalry the most daring of the Rangers,
which at times means the most reckless and stubborn. They are also known as
Tundra Riders and Mounties.

## The Code of the Tundra Rangers

- Keep the people of Canada safe, and keep the peace.
- See tyranny for what it is, whatever shape it takes, and stand against it.
- Help and protect those who need it, but leave them able to manage for
  themselves; that is the best help there is.
- Never let up in the pursuit of justice. The guilty answer for what they did.
- Welcome other beliefs and ways of living, and value what all peaceful,
  thinking beings share.
- Do not doubt the good being done. Believe in yourself and others will too.
- Make no threat or demand that you cannot and will not back with force.
- Keep your word and never betray a trust; the trust people give the Rangers
  is worth more than any reward.
- Never compromise a fellow Ranger, and never speak for another.
- One person can change things.
- No Tundra Ranger stands alone.

## GM Notes

Standard issue the sheet does not list, because the catalog has no row for it:
the energy rifle itself, a weapon for every W.P. with two E-Clips apiece, dress
boots, a pick-hatchet, a tundra survival kit, 20 climbing anchors, a small
M.D.C. ceramic mallet, a web vest and a winter cap. Many Rangers also wear a
multi-optics goggle, by special request.

Heavier weapons, armor, power armor, explosives, sensors, generators and
extra supplies may be issued for a particular assignment, at the commanding
officer''s discretion. Veterans collect personal non-standard gear as well.

Pay is 1500 credits a month on top of room, board, medical care and
equipment, and rises with rank and hazard duty (the book points at Coalition
War Campaign pages 50-54 for rank and pay). The sheet starts the character
with one month of salary.

A Ranger checks in at a station at least every two months and returns to
Regina or the Fort Smith headquarters at least once a year. Breaking the Code
or disobeying orders means a dishonorable discharge.

Mounts: the sheet offers a horse or a hovercycle. An exotic riding animal or
a bionic or robot horse (see Rifts New West) is the G.M.''s to give. Live
horses cannot be used through the winter; they founder in deep snow and
cannot stand prolonged freezing temperatures.

Simvan speak American/English at 80% rather than 98%, and Simvan,
Psi-Stalkers and other D-Bees read at 60% +1% per level rather than 84%.
Simvan and Psi-Stalker Cavalry Rangers use this O.C.C.''s skills in place of
their R.C.C. skills.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tundra-ranger-cavalry');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'tundra-ranger-cavalry';

